        "runtime:cd31d7a203120fe7",
        "runtime:d65cf4560be3f122"
      ],
      "upstreamResult": "An error a layout effect or ref callback throws outside any error boundary is rethrown by React's act(), where the case catches it.",
      "octaneResult": "Octane reports the error to the root's onUncaughtError, and the cases' roots record it there. The error, its message, and the editor cleanup assertions are upstream's.",
      "rationale": "Octane's documented root contract: with no boundary, effect-channel errors go to onUncaughtError (console.error by default) and the root unmounts; act() does not rethrow them.",
      "classification": "renderer-test-harness",
      "consumerImpact": "None for the components: the same errors are thrown from the same effects, and an application observes them through onUncaughtError or an error boundary.",
      "reviewCondition": "Review if Octane act() starts rethrowing effect-channel errors."
    },
